      "id": 1,
      "text": "Plains began as Horse Plains, a wintering spot for Native American horse herds that grazed on valley grasses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plains%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around a Northern Pacific Railroad station opened in 1883, making it a key rail stop in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plains%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1905 the U.S. Postal Service shortened the name to Plains, and the town was officially founded in 1907 under that name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plains%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Plains sits on the Clark Fork River, with its fairgrounds on one bank and the main town on the opposite shore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
